    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule: an owner's `membershipTier` becomes `GOLD` when their household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3 or more members after the create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\nThe tier is derived in `OwnerMapper` from data already carried on the `Owner`, and the mapper runs on both create and read (`GET /api/owners/{id}`). Since household size isn't derivable from existing fields, I persisted it at create time \u2014 mirroring how `namesakeCount` and `bulkSignupWarning` are already handled.\n\nChanges:\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `householdSize` field (`household_size` column) with getter/setter.\n- **Schema files** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `household_size INTEGER` column to the `owners` table.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, after computing `householdId`, set `householdSize` to the count of existing owners in that household plus one (this create). Added a documented `countHouseholdMembers` helper following the existing `countNamesakes` pattern.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `membershipTier` now returns `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise falls through to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum and updated the description.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` (third member of a shared household expects GOLD) passes, and the full suite builds green.",
